// Title: Sysmon Channel Reference Deletion
// ID: 18beca67-ab3e-4ee3-ba7a-a46ca8d7d0cc
// Status: test
// Level: high
// Author: Roberto Rodriguez (Cyb3rWard0g), OTR (Open Threat Research)
// Date: 2020-07-14
// Tags: attack.persistence, attack.defense-impairment, attack.t1112
// Description: Potential threat actor tampering with Sysmon manifest and eventually disabling it
// Converted by: Sigma Universal SIEM/EDR CLI

any where ((winlog.event_id == 4657 and (ObjectName like "*_WINEVT\\Publishers\\{5770385f-c22a-43e0-bf4c-06f5698ffbd9}*" or ObjectName like "*_WINEVT\\Channels\\Microsoft-Windows-Sysmon/Operational*") and ObjectValueName == "Enabled" and NewValue == 0) or (winlog.event_id == 4663 and (ObjectName like "*_WINEVT\\Publishers\\{5770385f-c22a-43e0-bf4c-06f5698ffbd9}*" or ObjectName like "*_WINEVT\\Channels\\Microsoft-Windows-Sysmon/Operational*") and AccessMask == "0x10000"))
